  "disable multi-thread when incx==0 or incy==0": 4,
  "In that case, the threads would be dependent.": 4,
  "for alignment": 4,
  "Quick return if possible.": 3,
  "Temporarily work-around the low performance issue with small input size &": 2,
  "multithreads.": 2,
  "void CNAME(enum CBLAS_ORDER order,\n\t   blasint m, blasint n,\n\t   FLOAT alpha,\n\t   FLOAT  *a, blasint": 2,
  "defined arm64": 2,
  "These were passed in as blasint, but the struct translates them to blaslong": 2,
  "Threshold chosen so that speed-up is > 1 on a Xeon E5-2630": 2,
  "**********************************************************\n * 2014-06-10 Saar\n * 2015-09-07 grisuthe": 2,
  "ABS & MAX": 2,
  "ABS & MIN": 2,
  "MAX": 2,
  "MIN": 2,
  "**********************************************************\n * 2014/06/09 Saar\n**********************": 2,
  "#ifdef SMP\n#ifdef __64BIT__\n#define SMPTEST 1\n#endif\n#endif": 2,
  "Multithreaded swap gives performance benefits in ThunderX2T99": 2,
  "Disable multi-threading as it does not show any performance": 2,
  "benefits. Keep the multi-threading code for the record.": 2,
  "CBLAS": 2,
  "unscaled": 2,
  "*****************************************************************\n 2014/06/07 Saar\n*****************": 1,
  "defined complex": 1,
  "defined CBLAS": 1,
  "defined dynarch": 1,
  "defined b/hfloat16": 1,
  "defined(__linux__) && defined(__x86_64__) && defined(BFLOAT16)": 1,
  "The gemv kernels in arm64/{gemv_n.S,gemv_n_sve.c,gemv_t.S,gemv_t_sve.c}": 1,
  "perform poorly in certain circumstances. We use the following boolean": 1,
  "variable along with the gemv argument values to avoid these inefficient": 1,
  "gemv cases, see github issue#4951.": 1,
  "GEMV transpose modes indexed by the GEMM transpose codes (N=0, T=1, R=2, C=3).": 1,
  "For real types only N and T occur. For complex types the OpenBLAS GEMV": 1,
  "extensions O, U, S and D (index 4..7) behave like N, T, R and C but": 1,
  "additionally conjugate the vector x, which lets a conjugated vector-shaped": 1,
  "operand of GEMM be handled without an explicit conjugation pass.": 1,
  "Even indices run on the GEMV_N kernels, odd indices on the GEMV_T kernels.": 1,
  "Check if we can convert GEMM -> GEMV": 1,
  "C = alpha * op(A) * op(B) + beta * C with op(B) a k x 1 vector: GEMV on A,": 1,
  "where a conjugated op(B) selects the x-conjugating modes.": 1,
  "C^T = op(B)^T * op(A)^T with op(A) a 1 x k vector: GEMV on B, where the": 1,
  "transposition swaps N<->T and R<->C, and a conjugated op(A) selects the": 1,
  "x-conjugating modes.": 1,
  "For LOONGARCH64, applying an offset to the buffer is essential": 1,
  "for minimizing cache conflicts and optimizing performance.": 1,
  "Every member shares M and N: an empty member means an empty batch.": 1,
  "[uplo][op(B)][op(A)], as in interface/gemm.c": 1,
  "Split the triangle into column ranges of equal area; every\n\t\t   thread then runs the single-threaded": 1,
  "Enables the New IMATCOPY code with inplace operation if lda == ldb": 1,
  "Test the input parameters.": 1,
  "Quick return if possible": 1,
  "*************************************************************************************\n* 2014/05/02 S": 1,
  "This can only happen through rounding: the\n\t\t\t\t   branch was chosen on ABS(dq1) > ABS(dq2),\n\t\t\t\t   w": 1,
  "Column Major": 1,
  "Row Major": 1,
  "end of the ifndef CBLAS ... else ... section": 1,
  "if ( args.m < 2 * GEMM_MULTITHREAD_THRESHOLD )\n\targs.nthreads = 1;\n  else\n\tif ( args.n < 2 * GEMM_MU": 1,
  "*********************************************************************\n 2014/06/07 Saar\n\n************": 1,
  "CREAL(*result) = 0.0;": 1,
  "CIMAG(*result) = 0.0;": 1,
  "cgemv_t.S return NaN if there are NaN or Inf in the buffer (see bug #746)": 1,
  "this is smallest dimension N of square input a to permit threading": 1,
  "see graph in issue #1820 for explanation": 1,
  "long double r;": 1,
  "scaled algorithm": 1,
  "no risk of intermediate overflow": 1,
  "scaled": 1,
  "use same scaling for both": 1,
  "intermediates might overflow": 1,
  "Calibrated on a Xeon E5-2630": 1,
  "It seems to be required for some K8 or Barcelona CPU": 1
